        "x2": 1170.0,
        "y2": 2175.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.5105506181716919,
      "reading_order": 10,
      "text": "4. (i) Extraction of yellow phosphorus $\\rightarrow$ Bone\ncharcoal\n(ii) Preparation of artificial diamonds $\\rightarrow$ Sugar\ncharcoal\n(iii) Gas masks $\\rightarrow$ Wood charcoal\n(iv) Moderator in nuclear reactors $\\rightarrow$ Graphite\n(v) Abrasive for cutting glass $\\rightarrow$ Diamond\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_a57b6c3c-dc4a-4dc6-aed6-d51df3870e67_9_block_010",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 244.0,
        "y1": 2204.0,
        "x2": 1171.0,
        "y2": 2665.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.27705565094947815,
      "reading_order": 11,
      "text": "5. (i) Passing CO gas over finely divided iron $\\rightarrow$\n$\\mathrm{M}(\\mathrm{CO})_5$ or $\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CO})_5$\n(ii) Passing $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ gas through powdered mag-\nnesium $\\rightarrow$ MO or MgO\n(iii) Heating $\\mathrm{M}_2\\mathrm{O}_3$ with CO $\\rightarrow$ M or Fe\n(iv) Passing $\\mathrm{CO}_2$ through sodium $\\rightarrow$ $\\mathrm{M}_2\\mathrm{CO}_3$ or\n$\\mathrm{Na}_2\\mathrm{CO}_3$\n\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260317_a57b6c3c-dc4a-4dc6-aed6-d51df3870e67_9_block_011",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1285.0,
